Welcome to the course! As your personal tutor, I will guide you through this journey from complete novice to a capable backend developer.
Here is your custom 12-Week PHP Web Development Syllabus. It is structured exactly like a professional tech bootcamp, balancing theoretical fundamentals with hands-on project builds.

🗺️ Phase 1: The Core Fundamentals (Weeks 1–4)

Goal: Understand how the web works and master basic programming logic using PHP.
• Week 1: Environment Setup & Your First Script
	• Installing local servers (XAMPP or Laravel Herd).
	• Configuring Visual Studio Code for PHP development.
	• Understanding how a server processes a .php file vs a static .html file.
	• Basic syntax, outputting data (echo, print), and adding comments.
• Week 2: Data Types, Variables, and Control Structures
	• Working with strings, integers, floats, and booleans.
	• Using conditional statements (if, else, elseif, switch).
	• Automating repetitive tasks with loops (while, do-while, for, foreach).
• Week 3: Complex Data & Code Organization
	• Mastering Arrays (Indexed, Associative, and Multi-dimensional).
	• Array manipulation functions (array_push, in_array, count).
	• Creating reusable code blocks with custom Functions (arguments, return values, type hinting).
• Week 4: Built-in Features & Web Interactivity
	• Using built-in superglobals ($_GET and $_POST) to capture user input.
	• Handling web forms and sanitizing data to prevent basic injection attacks.
	• Working with date/time functions and including external files (include, require).
🚀 Milestone Project 1: Build a dynamic Online Quiz Application or Tip Calculator that takes user inputs, processes them with PHP logic, and displays calculated results on the screen.

💾 Phase 2: Databases & Security (Weeks 5–8)

Goal: Connect your applications to a database and safely store user information.
• Week 5: Intro to MySQL Databases
	• Understanding relational databases and using phpMyAdmin.
	• Writing fundamental SQL queries: CREATE, SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE.
	• Setting up primary keys and understanding data types (VARCHAR, INT, TEXT).
• Week 6: PHP Data Objects (PDO)
	• Connecting PHP securely to MySQL using PDO (the industry standard).
	• Executing secure database operations using Prepared Statements to block SQL Injection.
	• Fetching database results and looping through them dynamically in HTML tables.
• Week 7: User Sessions & Authentication
	• Understanding stateless HTTP and managing state with $_SESSION and $_COOKIE.
	• Building a secure user registration system using PHP's password_hash() and password_verify().
	• Creating a user login and logout mechanism.
• Week 8: Restricting Access & Form Validation
	• Protecting specific dashboard pages from unauthenticated guests.
	• Advanced server-side form validation (e.g., checking for valid emails, enforcing password length).
	• Uploading files safely to the server (validating MIME types and sizes).
🚀 Milestone Project 2: Build a secure User Management System with registration, login, profile editing, and an administrative dashboard panel.

🏗️ Phase 3: Object-Oriented PHP & Architecture (Weeks 9–12)

Goal: Write clean, modular, and maintainable enterprise-level code.
• Week 9: Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) Basics
	• Moving away from procedural code into Classes and Objects.
	• Understanding properties, methods, and visibility modifiers (public, private, protected).
	• Using constructors (__construct) to initialize object states.
• Week 10: Advanced OOP Concepts
	• Implementing Inheritance to share functionality between classes.
	• Using Interfaces and Abstract Classes to create code blueprints.
	• Working with static methods and namespaces to organize large applications.
• Week 11: The MVC Architecture & Dependency Management
	• Understanding the Model-View-Controller pattern.
	• Using Composer to manage external third-party PHP packages.
	• Setting up clean URLs using basic routing and .htaccess rewrites.
• Week 12: Framework Integration (Introduction to Laravel)
	• How modern industry projects use PHP.
	• Installing Laravel and mapping your raw PHP knowledge to a framework ecosystem.
	• Final project optimization, debugging, and deployment strategies.
🎓 Final Graduation Project: Build a full-fledged, object-oriented Content Management System (CMS) or a mini E-commerce Store with product management, shopping cart logic, and a multi-user database system.
